WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.200
-Our first guest
is an Emmy-nominated actor

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:06.167
and a very funny comedian
starring in the new film

00:00:06.167 --> 00:00:09.567
"Home Team," which premieres
on Netflix tomorrow.

00:00:09.567 --> 00:00:12.434
Here's the always entertaining
Kevin James,

00:00:12.434 --> 00:00:13.434
ladies and gentlemen.

00:00:13.434 --> 00:00:14.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.534 --> 00:00:18.133
Yeah!
Kevin James!

00:00:18.133 --> 00:00:20.601
Oh, I love you, buddy.

00:00:20.601 --> 00:00:22.701
-Love you too, man.
-Welcome.

00:00:22.701 --> 00:00:25.367
Welcome back to the show.
You look good, pal.

00:00:25.367 --> 00:00:26.501
I don't know if I've ever --

00:00:26.501 --> 00:00:29.767
Have I ever seen you
with a shaved head?

00:00:29.767 --> 00:00:31.100
-Oh, yeah, I don't know.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:32.767
This is the first time on there
with a shaved head.

00:00:32.767 --> 00:00:37.200
I did a movie, which was, like,
a little sinister movie,

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.567
called "Becky," and it was
a different character,

00:00:39.567 --> 00:00:40.934
so I shaved my head.

00:00:40.934 --> 00:00:42.834
And then I was like,
"I'll, uh --

00:00:42.834 --> 00:00:44.267
I'll just grow it back
afterwards."

00:00:44.267 --> 00:00:46.801
And I started to grow it back,
and God stepped in and was like,

00:00:46.801 --> 00:00:50.334
"Yeah, it's not gonna happen."
It didn't come in very thick.

00:00:50.334 --> 00:00:52.701
So, I was like, "Ooh, maybe
I better stick with this."

00:00:52.701 --> 00:00:54.767
You have good hair.
-Thank you.

00:00:54.767 --> 00:00:56.400
Yeah, this is --
-Very good hair.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:59.033
-Thank you. This is the best
toupee money can buy.

00:00:59.033 --> 00:01:00.367
I mean, you can really --
-It really is.

00:01:00.367 --> 00:01:02.000
-Yeah, the glue --
-It's tight on the side.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:03.767
I like it.
-Yeah.

00:01:03.767 --> 00:01:06.100
Well, it's a new year.
You got a new look.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:08.000
I mean, are you doing
anything else differently

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.501
for the new year?

00:01:09.501 --> 00:01:11.567
-I'm trying, as always,
to get in shape,

00:01:11.567 --> 00:01:13.133
but it's just --
it's not working

00:01:13.133 --> 00:01:14.934
'cause I'm older than you, man.

00:01:14.934 --> 00:01:16.868
I'm just feeling --
I feel everything.

00:01:16.868 --> 00:01:20.000
You know, the aches and pains
and just moving around.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.434
I can't get motivated.
You know, it's even --

00:01:22.434 --> 00:01:24.767
even getting out of bed
takes me, like --

00:01:24.767 --> 00:01:26.934
I used to spring up.
But I don't know.

00:01:26.934 --> 00:01:29.501
It takes me --
First of all, I have a mattress,

00:01:29.501 --> 00:01:32.200
I've had it for like 10 years,
so it kind of knows me.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:35.434
You know what I'm saying?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.434 --> 00:01:38.634
Got, like, the fat-guy divot
right in the middle.

00:01:38.634 --> 00:01:40.033
You know what I'm talking about?

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:45.133
Like, if you walked
in my bedroom in the morning

00:01:45.133 --> 00:01:47.501
and you --
You ever see half an avocado?

00:01:47.501 --> 00:01:48.567
It would literally look like...

00:01:48.567 --> 00:01:50.868
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.868 --> 00:01:52.801
Yeah.
-The pit, yeah.

00:01:52.801 --> 00:01:55.100
-I'm just
kind of stuck in there.

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:57.801
It takes me -- So that takes
a while to get going.

00:01:57.801 --> 00:02:01.567
-Yeah, I sometimes --
I almost sometimes rock myself

00:02:01.567 --> 00:02:04.234
to go like -- "hoo-ya"
and then get up.

00:02:04.234 --> 00:02:05.267
-Yeah.
-And get out.

00:02:05.267 --> 00:02:07.601
-A momentum thing to get out.

00:02:07.601 --> 00:02:10.200
For me, even to get to the side,
because I sleep in the middle,

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:14.534
to get over, I got to get enough
weight over the side of the bed.

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:16.901
It's like -- You remember that
arcade game where the coins

00:02:16.901 --> 00:02:18.300
where they just keep pushing it
closer to the side?

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:19.734
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.734 --> 00:02:27.667
Until you spill onto the floor
like a baby calf being born.

00:02:27.667 --> 00:02:29.534
-How are the --
How are the kids?

00:02:29.534 --> 00:02:33.234
You ever work out with the kids?
You do active stuff with them?

00:02:33.234 --> 00:02:34.934
-I try to.
You know, I mean,

00:02:34.934 --> 00:02:36.834
the shutdown, for us,
was miserable, you know?

00:02:36.834 --> 00:02:38.934
And kids now --

00:02:38.934 --> 00:02:40.601
You have how many kids?
-I have two girls.

00:02:40.601 --> 00:02:42.734
-Three? Two.
-Yeah, two.

00:02:42.734 --> 00:02:44.734
-They're probably active little
girls -- I don't know why.

00:02:44.734 --> 00:02:47.968
I've got a boy --
just not active.

00:02:47.968 --> 00:02:51.000
I try to get him going.
He's just --

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:52.801
Kids today, it feels like

00:02:52.801 --> 00:02:53.968
they're less active
than we were.

00:02:53.968 --> 00:02:55.434
I mean --
And I said, "Hey, we gotta

00:02:55.434 --> 00:02:56.667
start working out, buddy."

00:02:56.667 --> 00:02:58.601
And he's always --
it's always the video games.

00:02:58.601 --> 00:03:02.067
And so I said, "Enough of that.
You can't do that anymore."

00:03:02.067 --> 00:03:03.334
And he just tries to negotiate
his way out of it.

00:03:03.334 --> 00:03:04.467
He's like,
"I don't want to do --

00:03:04.467 --> 00:03:05.667
Can we please -- Can I --"
and I'm like,

00:03:05.667 --> 00:03:07.100
"No, we gotta do
something active, me and you.

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:08.434
Let's go.
We're going."

00:03:08.434 --> 00:03:10.000
And he's like,
"What if I got --" he said this.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:11.667
"What if I got an Oculus?"

00:03:11.667 --> 00:03:13.000
And I didn't know what
an Oculus was,

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:16.634
but it's one of those
virtual-reality masks.

00:03:16.634 --> 00:03:18.601
-Yeah.
-And he was like,

00:03:18.601 --> 00:03:20.067
"What if I get --"
because you can do things,

00:03:20.067 --> 00:03:22.100
he says, on that
where you can be active.

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:24.834
He says, you can -- there are
boxing games on there

00:03:24.834 --> 00:03:29.133
where you can box Apollo Creed
and Rocky or Muhammad Ali.

00:03:29.133 --> 00:03:30.767
And there's sword games
where you're like a pirate

00:03:30.767 --> 00:03:32.133
and all that stuff.

00:03:32.133 --> 00:03:34.400
So, he's like, "I'll be active.
There's dance stuff."

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:35.968
And I said, "All right.

00:03:35.968 --> 00:03:38.400
Well, maybe that would be
all right, I guess."

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:42.634
So, I let him get the Oculus.
And I swear to you, Jimmy,

00:03:42.634 --> 00:03:44.267
there's a lot of things we do --

00:03:44.267 --> 00:03:47.367
We talk about
and we embellish stories.

00:03:47.367 --> 00:03:50.634
I wish I was making this up
about my kid.

00:03:50.634 --> 00:03:53.000
Ready?
The first day he has it,

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.234
I walk down the steps.

00:03:54.234 --> 00:03:55.767
I come down the steps,
I see him in the foyer.

00:03:55.767 --> 00:03:58.334
He's standing with the mask
on -- the Oculus, right?

00:03:58.334 --> 00:04:00.901
And he's literally just
standing there for 10 minutes,

00:04:00.901 --> 00:04:03.167
just nothing.
And then, every once in a while,

00:04:03.167 --> 00:04:07.267
I'll just see this.
I'll just see...

00:04:07.267 --> 00:04:09.801
with his fingers.
And he did nothing.

00:04:09.801 --> 00:04:11.901
And he goes like this, nothing.
10 minutes.

00:04:11.901 --> 00:04:13.601
And I go,
"He doesn't look like

00:04:13.601 --> 00:04:15.400
he's fighting
Apollo Creed at all."

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:17.467
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.467 --> 00:04:19.300
"This is not happening."
-No.

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:20.434
-I literally -- I rip it off.

00:04:20.434 --> 00:04:21.667
I'm like,
"What are you watching?

00:04:21.667 --> 00:04:23.634
What are you doing?"
I'm --

00:04:23.634 --> 00:04:27.200
He downloaded a job simulator
virtual reality --

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:28.834
He got a job
at a convenience store,

00:04:28.834 --> 00:04:30.467
and that's all he was doing.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.467 --> 00:04:32.501
He was waiting for customers
to come in.

00:04:32.501 --> 00:04:34.033
I'm not making it up, Jimmy.

00:04:34.033 --> 00:04:37.934
I swear --
And he was ringing people up.

00:04:37.934 --> 00:04:39.434
That's all he was --
He's getting, like, cigarettes,

00:04:39.434 --> 00:04:40.901
and then he would
hand it to them.

00:04:40.901 --> 00:04:43.634
And then he would sit there
and wait for the next customer.

00:04:43.634 --> 00:04:45.133
He just sat there.
Literally...

00:04:45.133 --> 00:04:48.300
[ Laughter ]
...nothing.

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:50.467
-Why didn't he pick
a different job?

00:04:50.467 --> 00:04:52.701
-Pick up a mop at least!

00:04:52.701 --> 00:04:53.868
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.868 --> 00:04:55.133
Stack some cases of beer!

00:04:55.133 --> 00:04:57.667
-Mop up the fake --
-Yes!

00:04:57.667 --> 00:04:58.701
He's sitting there.

00:04:58.701 --> 00:05:00.467
He's a horrible business guy,
too.

00:05:00.467 --> 00:05:02.400
He's scratching off
his own lotto tickets.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:04.467
He's ruining everything.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.467 --> 00:05:07.834
Very lazy kid.

00:05:07.834 --> 00:05:10.934
-We gotta talk about
your new movie, "Home Team."

00:05:10.934 --> 00:05:12.300
It's funny, as always.

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:14.834
Kevin James, is so, so funny.
But it's heartwarming.

00:05:14.834 --> 00:05:16.601
It's something
the whole family can enjoy.

00:05:16.601 --> 00:05:19.434
It's on Netflix.
Based on a true story.

00:05:19.434 --> 00:05:21.100
Can you set up --
-Yes.

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:23.234
-Set up what the movie
is about for everyone.

00:05:23.234 --> 00:05:26.968
-Yeah, Sean Payton, who is the
coach of the New Orleans Saints,

00:05:26.968 --> 00:05:29.234
after winning the Super Bowl,
he got suspended.

00:05:29.234 --> 00:05:31.567
It was that bounty gate
a long time ago.

00:05:31.567 --> 00:05:33.767
And he got suspended for a year

00:05:33.767 --> 00:05:36.567
where he couldn't be associated
with anybody in the NFL.

00:05:36.567 --> 00:05:39.334
And I never knew this.
I heard about the suspension,

00:05:39.334 --> 00:05:40.501
and I didn't know
what happened with it.

00:05:40.501 --> 00:05:44.467
But he spent
that entire next year

00:05:44.467 --> 00:05:48.100
coaching his 12-year-old son's
football team, the Warriors,

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:49.968
and he brought them
to a championship.

00:05:49.968 --> 00:05:51.734
And he reconnected with his son,

00:05:51.734 --> 00:05:54.601
and he brought them all the way
to the championship game.

00:05:54.601 --> 00:05:57.133
And he lost the championship,
but it was an amazing --

00:05:57.133 --> 00:06:00.400
He says it was the best year
of football in his life

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:01.767
because he connected
with his son.

00:06:01.767 --> 00:06:04.567
And I disagree with him
because he won a Super Bowl.

00:06:04.567 --> 00:06:07.334
It's pretty cool.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:07.334 --> 00:06:08.634
Let's be honest, right?

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:10.167
The kid's great,
but that's second place.

00:06:10.167 --> 00:06:13.000
[ Laughter ]

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:14.300
Right?
It's a Super Bowl, man.

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:16.567
-No, no, no.
The more important is that,

00:06:16.567 --> 00:06:17.901
yeah, he connected.
-Yes.

00:06:17.901 --> 00:06:19.000
-You guys got to see this.
It's great.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:20.033
I want to show a clip.

00:06:20.033 --> 00:06:21.934
Here's Kevin James
in "Home Team."

00:06:21.934 --> 00:06:23.300
Take a look at this.

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:25.801
-He's at the 20!
He's at the 10!

00:06:25.801 --> 00:06:28.567
Oh, my God!
Touchdown, Warriors!

00:06:28.567 --> 00:06:34.234
[ Cheering ]

00:06:34.234 --> 00:06:36.400
First touchdown of the season!

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:41.400
And just as the game
comes to an end.

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:43.567
-That was a touchdown!
It was a touchdown!

00:06:43.567 --> 00:06:45.000
-Take it easy.
Act like you've been here.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:48.801
-Yeah!
Booyah!

00:06:48.801 --> 00:06:50.634
And, folks, that'll do it.

00:06:50.634 --> 00:06:56.334
Final score here --
Warriors 6, Knights 38.

00:06:56.334 --> 00:06:59.434
-We got a touchdown!
We got a touchdown!

00:06:59.434 --> 00:07:02.634
We got a touchdown!
We got a touchdown!

00:07:02.701 --> 00:07:05.901
We got a touchdown!
We got a touchdown!

00:07:05.901 --> 00:07:07.434
[ Applause ]

00:07:07.434 --> 00:07:10.200
-"We scored a touchdown!
We scored a --"

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:11.667
Kevin James, everybody.

00:07:11.667 --> 00:07:13.934
"Home Team" premieres tomorrow.

00:07:13.934 --> 00:07:15.667
Tomorrow on Netflix,
"Home Team."

00:07:15.667 --> 00:07:17.400
More fun with Kevin
when we come back.

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:18.467
Stick around, everybody.

